msgid "SoC refinement and physical acceptance"
msgstr "SoC refinement and physical acceptance"

msgid "Nexus maintains exact silicon mechanisms. SoC facts and routes, private provider implementations, generated static instances, Board connections and observed physical behavior have separate responsibilities. The existing typed factory and shared readonly operations tables remain the runtime interface; no new registry, worker, allocator, lock or product configuration authority is introduced."
msgstr "Nexus maintains exact silicon mechanisms. SoC facts and routes, private provider implementations, generated static instances, Board connections and observed physical behavior have separate responsibilities. The existing typed factory and shared readonly operations tables remain the runtime interface; no new registry, worker, allocator, lock or product configuration authority is introduced."

msgid "The {download}`55-item execution ledger <soc-refinement-execution.csv>` separates existing correction and optimization (SOC-01–27), conditional target extensions (SOC-28–36), and physical acceptance (SOC-37–55). Codex owns all maintenance. Implementation status, executed software evidence and physical status are recorded independently. An authored plan, a synthetic parser test or an ARM link cannot complete a physical exit condition."
msgstr "The {download}`55-item execution ledger <soc-refinement-execution.csv>` separates existing correction and optimization (SOC-01–27), conditional target extensions (SOC-28–36), and physical acceptance (SOC-37–55). Codex owns all maintenance. Implementation status, executed software evidence and physical status are recorded independently. An authored plan, a synthetic parser test or an ARM link cannot complete a physical exit condition."

msgid "Current software boundaries"
msgstr "Current software boundaries"

msgid "STM32F407VET6/ZGT6 and GD32F470ZGT6 maintain reviewed fixed clock, startup, monotonic timer and selected controller modes. The [derived capability matrix](../delivery/capabilities.md) enumerates exact facts, routes, selected production sources and software fixtures. Exact F103RB/GD303RC references add legacy channel-DMA UART, IRQ-message I2C and physical Flash, single-shot ADC and fixed PWM. G474 adds selected bulb ADC shots/finite TIM6 DMA, polling I2C and ECC Flash to its GPIO/UART/SPI/PWM/EXTI/watchdog baseline. The non-M4 references are STM32H743ZIT6 and STM32U575ZIT6Q. H743 maintains fixed clock/cache profiles, finite UART DMA TX or RX-IDLE, optional initialized D2 SRAM1 and selected finite peripherals. Separate V/HSI64 baremetal selections add AXI-SRAM continuous USART3 RX and explicit duplex DMA. U575 keeps its TZEN0 finite peripherals separate from an independent copied GPIO dual-world reference. CPU ABI/runtime support for other Cortex-M profiles does not imply a full SoC, Board or peripheral implementation."
msgstr "STM32F407VET6/ZGT6 and GD32F470ZGT6 maintain reviewed fixed clock, startup, monotonic timer and selected controller modes. The [derived capability matrix](../delivery/capabilities.md) enumerates exact facts, routes, selected production sources and software fixtures. Exact F103RB/GD303RC references add legacy channel-DMA UART, IRQ-message I2C and physical Flash, single-shot ADC and fixed PWM. G474 adds selected bulb ADC shots/finite TIM6 DMA, polling I2C and ECC Flash to its GPIO/UART/SPI/PWM/EXTI/watchdog baseline. The non-M4 references are STM32H743ZIT6 and STM32U575ZIT6Q. H743 maintains fixed clock/cache profiles, finite UART DMA TX or RX-IDLE, optional initialized D2 SRAM1 and selected finite peripherals. Separate V/HSI64 baremetal selections add AXI-SRAM continuous USART3 RX and explicit duplex DMA. U575 keeps its TZEN0 finite peripherals separate from an independent copied GPIO dual-world reference. CPU ABI/runtime support for other Cortex-M profiles does not imply a full SoC, Board or peripheral implementation."

msgid "The [five bounded I/O increments](io-extension-boundaries.md) add common mapped ownership with coherent Native NOR, an AMP epoch/cache core, exact F407 masked Flash handoff, U575 prepared-LSE RTC RUN polling and frame contracts with an optional exact H743 RGB565 DMA2D component. Their public targets do not establish unselected hardware providers, full original exits or physical qualification."
msgstr "The [five bounded I/O increments](io-extension-boundaries.md) add common mapped ownership with coherent Native NOR, an AMP epoch/cache core, exact F407 masked Flash handoff, U575 prepared-LSE RTC RUN polling and frame contracts with an optional exact H743 RGB565 DMA2D component. Their public targets do not establish unselected hardware providers, full original exits or physical qualification."

msgid "The [U575 retained-clock and Stop2 reference](u575-retained-time.md) adds an independent RTC elapsed domain and an explicit masked WUT/Stop2 owner, with closed/joined RUN owners, verified MSIS4 access restoration and real cleanup. This is an exact TZEN0 baremetal software subset. Default Core TIM2 deadlines remain invalid after stop. LPDMA/LPBAM, physical retention/accuracy/current/wake acceptance and the full SOC-35 exit remain open."
msgstr "The [U575 retained-clock and Stop2 reference](u575-retained-time.md) adds an independent RTC elapsed domain and an explicit masked WUT/Stop2 owner, with closed/joined RUN owners, verified MSIS4 access restoration and real cleanup. This is an exact TZEN0 baremetal software subset. Default Core TIM2 deadlines remain invalid after stop. LPDMA/LPBAM, physical retention/accuracy/current/wake acceptance and the full SOC-35 exit remain open."

