msgid "These are source-reviewed Board references. Their physical PCB revisions, silicon revisions, solder bridges, electrical connections and option bytes have not been observed. Reference-only HIL admission fails closed; selecting a matching chip name cannot promote a reference into a qualified physical Board. The [extension execution record](../delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md) distinguishes normal commit gates, development ARM observations and final qualification. The [earlier baseline](../delivery/soc-refinement-verification.md) retains its original source identity and evidence. Reference software status in the ledger records bounded host/ARM evidence; it does not establish a clean candidate, physical acceptance or every original exit condition."
msgstr "These are source-reviewed Board references. Their physical PCB revisions, silicon revisions, solder bridges, electrical connections and option bytes have not been observed. Reference-only HIL admission fails closed; selecting a matching chip name cannot promote a reference into a qualified physical Board. The [extension execution record](../delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md) distinguishes normal commit gates, development ARM observations and final qualification. The [earlier baseline](../delivery/soc-refinement-verification.md) retains its original source identity and evidence. Reference software status in the ledger records bounded host/ARM evidence; it does not establish a clean candidate, physical acceptance or every original exit condition."

msgid "The [G474 contract](stm32g474.md) describes independent EXTI0/PA0 and EXTI1/PA1 rings, pending-bit acknowledgement, mux/gate ownership and source withdrawal. Its test Board is an explicit software fixture, with no inferred connector, button or electrical bias. The [H743 contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32h743/README.md) defines all four HSI 32/64 MHz and Cache off/on combinations. Fixed cold profile selection does not implement a running frequency transition."
msgstr "The [G474 contract](stm32g474.md) describes independent EXTI0/PA0 and EXTI1/PA1 rings, pending-bit acknowledgement, mux/gate ownership and source withdrawal. Its test Board is an explicit software fixture, with no inferred connector, button or electrical bias. The [H743 contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32h743/README.md) defines all four HSI 32/64 MHz and Cache off/on combinations. Fixed cold profile selection does not implement a running frequency transition."

msgid "H743 USART3 DMA TX owns DMA1 Stream0, DMAMUX1 Channel0 request46 and its separate vector; the alternative RX-IDLE selection owns DMA1 Stream1/channel1 request45 and keeps TX IRQ-driven. Finite RX needs owner service and rearm gaps; it is not continuous or implicit duplex. Cache-on buffers occupy exclusively owned complete 32-byte lines in selected initialized AXI/SRAM1, with no outward rounding or hidden bounce buffer. Cache cleaning follows borrow admission, runs outside the long interrupt mask, and cannot settle storage while preparation is active. DMA completion, wire TC and source withdrawal remain distinct. Failed withdrawal quarantines the loan; the provider must drain before cache and timer shutdown."
msgstr "H743 USART3 DMA TX owns DMA1 Stream0, DMAMUX1 Channel0 request46 and its separate vector; the alternative RX-IDLE selection owns DMA1 Stream1/channel1 request45 and keeps TX IRQ-driven. Finite RX needs owner service and rearm gaps; it is not continuous or implicit duplex. Cache-on buffers occupy exclusively owned complete 32-byte lines in selected initialized AXI/SRAM1, with no outward rounding or hidden bounce buffer. Cache cleaning follows borrow admission, runs outside the long interrupt mask, and cannot settle storage while preparation is active. DMA completion, wire TC and source withdrawal remain distinct. Failed withdrawal quarantines the loan; the provider must drain before cache and timer shutdown."

msgid "The [U575 dual-world contract](u575-trustzone-contract.md) is an independent no-OS integration fixture. Its cold owner observes provisioned option bytes, checks actual physical permissions, clears future shared RAM, then configures and seals attribution. A real SG gateway authenticates the NS world rather than an untrusted task identity, checks CMSE permissions and copies a bounded request through the existing GPIO broker. The layout and GPIO grant belong to the reference fixture, not to reusable platform policy. A separate copied job entry admits up to eight PC7 commands into one Secure slot, advances one command per SERVICE and uses nonwrapping tickets; no NS pointer survives return. No option-byte programming, RTOS isolation, general factory integration or asynchronous transport is claimed."
msgstr "The [U575 dual-world contract](u575-trustzone-contract.md) is an independent no-OS integration fixture. Its cold owner observes provisioned option bytes, checks actual physical permissions, clears future shared RAM, then configures and seals attribution. A real SG gateway authenticates the NS world rather than an untrusted task identity, checks CMSE permissions and copies a bounded request through the existing GPIO broker. The layout and GPIO grant belong to the reference fixture, not to reusable platform policy. A separate copied job entry admits up to eight PC7 commands into one Secure slot, advances one command per SERVICE and uses nonwrapping tickets; no NS pointer survives return. No option-byte programming, RTOS isolation, general factory integration or asynchronous transport is claimed."

msgid "Clock bootstrap uses finite poll work bounds before the final clock exists; polls are not measured elapsed milliseconds. Cleanup must distinguish remaining recovery obligations from conservative settings allowed to remain. The monotonic timer belongs to one successfully started boot domain. The 32-bit references and GD303 hardware cascade require high-overflow service within 2^32 nominal microseconds; F103's 16-bit TIM2 requires 65.536 ms. Old deadlines cannot be carried across stop/restart. NMI/HardFault, paused timers, dynamic PLL changes and deep STOP require their own exact contract rather than assumptions from ordinary task execution."
msgstr "Clock bootstrap uses finite poll work bounds before the final clock exists; polls are not measured elapsed milliseconds. Cleanup must distinguish remaining recovery obligations from conservative settings allowed to remain. The monotonic timer belongs to one successfully started boot domain. The 32-bit references and GD303 hardware cascade require high-overflow service within 2^32 nominal microseconds; F103's 16-bit TIM2 requires 65.536 ms. Old deadlines cannot be carried across stop/restart. NMI/HardFault, paused timers, dynamic PLL changes and deep STOP require their own exact contract rather than assumptions from ordinary task execution."

msgid "Cold admission rejects observable foreign selected owners before global clock mutation. Generated pin admission observes all required GPIO gates and validates all selected pin modes and locks before capturing or changing any pin. This includes controller routes and hidden endpoint CS pins; an unrelated shared-bank pin does not become owned. An initialization failure includes its partially initialized object in reverse cleanup. Failed readback preserves exactly the remaining cleanup responsibility instead of returning a successful release."
msgstr "Cold admission rejects observable foreign selected owners before global clock mutation. Generated pin admission observes all required GPIO gates and validates all selected pin modes and locks before capturing or changing any pin. This includes controller routes and hidden endpoint CS pins; an unrelated shared-bank pin does not become owned. An initialization failure includes its partially initialized object in reverse cleanup. Failed readback preserves exactly the remaining cleanup responsibility instead of returning a successful release."

msgid "The timer start transaction clears stale UIF, observes a fresh UG update, clears that flag and verifies CNT before publishing the epoch. Runtime overflow advances the epoch only after acknowledged UIF. A refused ACK invalidates public time, records the private timer fault and attempts finite source/clocked-counter/NVIC withdrawal. This loss of the deadline domain is always terminal, including successful source isolation: the CPU preserves a terminal interrupt mask, invokes the existing bounded fault observer and parks if that observer returns. No invalid zero timestamp resumes a deadline consumer, and no request or low-power loan is released. Products may provide separately reviewed non-returning recovery. Ordinary stop/restart and cleanup retry belong to normal lifecycle control; they do not resume this terminal path. A snapshot rechecks epoch validity under the same saved interrupt mask used to read both counter words."
msgstr "The timer start transaction clears stale UIF, observes a fresh UG update, clears that flag and verifies CNT before publishing the epoch. Runtime overflow advances the epoch only after acknowledged UIF. A refused ACK invalidates public time, records the private timer fault and attempts finite source/clocked-counter/NVIC withdrawal. This loss of the deadline domain is always terminal, including successful source isolation: the CPU preserves a terminal interrupt mask, invokes the existing bounded fault observer and parks if that observer returns. No invalid zero timestamp resumes a deadline consumer, and no request or low-power loan is released. Products may provide separately reviewed non-returning recovery. Ordinary stop/restart and cleanup retry belong to normal lifecycle control; they do not resume this terminal path. A snapshot rechecks epoch validity under the same saved interrupt mask used to read both counter words."

msgid "`.noinit` means startup neither copies nor clears those bytes. It does not prove retention through a particular reset, power event or sleep mode. CPU reachability, DMA reachability, linker placement and physical retention are separate facts. Factory access does not initialize or reacquire any of these resources."
msgstr "`.noinit` means startup neither copies nor clears those bytes. It does not prove retention through a particular reset, power event or sleep mode. CPU reachability, DMA reachability, linker placement and physical retention are separate facts. Factory access does not initialize or reacquire any of these resources."

msgid "IRQ and DMA routines have finite work contracts. The selected execution owner must continue required service/cancel/drain progress. DMA completion, wire completion and withdrawal of every request reference precede SETTLED. Failed withdrawal retains QUARANTINED storage; cancellation is not permission to reclaim it. Continuous block providers stop on exhausted replacement storage and never write consumer-owned blocks or invent exact missed-event counts."
msgstr "IRQ and DMA routines have finite work contracts. The selected execution owner must continue required service/cancel/drain progress. DMA completion, wire completion and withdrawal of every request reference precede SETTLED. Failed withdrawal retains QUARANTINED storage; cancellation is not permission to reclaim it. Continuous block providers stop on exhausted replacement storage and never write consumer-owned blocks or invent exact missed-event counts."

msgid "Public typed I/O contracts belong under `io/include`; cross-chip controller algorithms have private headers and implementation targets. SoC wrappers own silicon layout/bit assertions and physical IRQ/DMA/clock bindings. Shared code placement follows those dependencies. CMake owns source selection, and resolver facts own configuration identity; moving a file does not create a second graph."
msgstr "Public typed I/O contracts belong under `io/include`; cross-chip controller algorithms have private headers and implementation targets. SoC wrappers own silicon layout/bit assertions and physical IRQ/DMA/clock bindings. Shared code placement follows those dependencies. CMake owns source selection, and resolver facts own configuration identity; moving a file does not create a second graph."

