msgid "F407 CCM is CPU-only and rejected as a DMA buffer. H743 memory facts describe DMA1/DMA2, BDMA and MDMA separately. The implemented finite USART3 DMA1 TX/RX lanes admit selected, initialized AXI SRAM or explicitly budgeted D2 SRAM1; unselected domains, TCM and an unready SRAM1 gate are rejected. MDMA reachability to TCM does not authorize a driver, cache protocol or linker placement. U575 has separate finite USART1 GPDMA TX and hardware-chain TX selections in SRAM1. The finite chain implements real node fetch and drain; it does not provide generic scatter/gather, circular/RX chains, LPDMA or security-crossing DMA. Its synchronous CPU gateway does not authorize DMA buffers or asynchronous storage loans. Legacy `dma` facts and explicit `dma_engines` are alternative authored forms; contradictory inputs are rejected rather than repaired."
msgstr "F407 CCM is CPU-only and rejected as a DMA buffer. H743 memory facts describe DMA1/DMA2, BDMA and MDMA separately. The implemented finite USART3 DMA1 TX/RX lanes admit selected, initialized AXI SRAM or explicitly budgeted D2 SRAM1; unselected domains, TCM and an unready SRAM1 gate are rejected. MDMA reachability to TCM does not authorize a driver, cache protocol or linker placement. U575 has separate finite USART1 GPDMA TX and hardware-chain TX selections in SRAM1. The finite chain implements real node fetch and drain; it does not provide generic scatter/gather, circular/RX chains, LPDMA or security-crossing DMA. Its synchronous CPU gateway does not authorize DMA buffers or asynchronous storage loans. Legacy `dma` facts and explicit `dma_engines` are alternative authored forms; contradictory inputs are rejected rather than repaired."

msgid "SDK identity includes reviewed original CMSIS Device files, their licenses, upstream revisions and the selected family payload. Verification checks bytes, file sets and observed filesystem identity across its read window. A successful check is not an atomic filesystem snapshot; actual consumers must use the same immutable SDK. Independent installed consumers must exercise the public platform interface without inheriting private vendor include paths."
msgstr "SDK identity includes reviewed original CMSIS Device files, their licenses, upstream revisions and the selected family payload. Verification checks bytes, file sets and observed filesystem identity across its read window. A successful check is not an atomic filesystem snapshot; actual consumers must use the same immutable SDK. Independent installed consumers must exercise the public platform interface without inheriting private vendor include paths."

msgid "Hot-path observations retain actual ELF bytes, resolved selection, compile flags, tool identities, resources and complete command receipts. A changed Board route, CPU/ABI, backend, clock, memory domain or capacity makes a regression comparison incomparable. Empty-to-selected image growth is reported as a selection cost, not as an equivalent-profile performance improvement. Physical cycles, maximum interrupt blackout and worst-case service intervals remain unmeasured."
msgstr "Hot-path observations retain actual ELF bytes, resolved selection, compile flags, tool identities, resources and complete command receipts. A changed Board route, CPU/ABI, backend, clock, memory domain or capacity makes a regression comparison incomparable. Empty-to-selected image growth is reported as a selection cost, not as an equivalent-profile performance improvement. Physical cycles, maximum interrupt blackout and worst-case service intervals remain unmeasured."

msgid "Physical preparation and execution"
msgstr "Physical preparation and execution"

msgid "`tools/hil/soc_acceptance.py plan` prepares all nineteen physical obligations without touching equipment. Each case contains required hardware, stimulation, raw observations, assertions, safety actions, metric units, unreviewed null limits and an exit condition. Selection gaps and unsupported OS cases remain explicit. The result is always `prepared_unbound` / `not_executed`."
msgstr "`tools/hil/soc_acceptance.py plan` prepares all nineteen physical obligations without touching equipment. Each case contains required hardware, stimulation, raw observations, assertions, safety actions, metric units, unreviewed null limits and an exit condition. Selection gaps and unsupported OS cases remain explicit. The result is always `prepared_unbound` / `not_executed`."

msgid "A real station supplies observed PCB revision, part/UID, probe, supply, wiring, exact ELF, resolved configuration, recomputed resources and reviewed workload. Existing `admit.py` establishes that admission. A station-authored SoC protocol binds one case, selected controller IDs, required instruments/calibration bytes, stimulation and numeric limits. Invariant failure counts must remain exactly zero; actual work counts/durations require a positive reviewed lower bound. Nothing in the repository supplies product acceptance numbers or fabricates pin wiring."
msgstr "A real station supplies observed PCB revision, part/UID, probe, supply, wiring, exact ELF, resolved configuration, recomputed resources and reviewed workload. Existing `admit.py` establishes that admission. A station-authored SoC protocol binds one case, selected controller IDs, required instruments/calibration bytes, stimulation and numeric limits. Invariant failure counts must remain exactly zero; actual work counts/durations require a positive reviewed lower bound. Nothing in the repository supplies product acceptance numbers or fabricates pin wiring."

msgid "`capture` delegates to the maintained acquisition runner. The existing six operations retain exact tool/input identities, exclusive station ownership, whole-argument argv without a shell, timeout/output bounds, cleanup and quarantine. The serial/instrument adapter must receive and content-pin the SoC protocol and all instrument records. This runner does not implement automatic waveform, CAN/USB/Ethernet peers or power interruption; station-owned adapters provide those operations. A successful capture is only `executed_unqualified`."
msgstr "`capture` delegates to the maintained acquisition runner. The existing six operations retain exact tool/input identities, exclusive station ownership, whole-argument argv without a shell, timeout/output bounds, cleanup and quarantine. The serial/instrument adapter must receive and content-pin the SoC protocol and all instrument records. This runner does not implement automatic waveform, CAN/USB/Ethernet peers or power interruption; station-owned adapters provide those operations. A successful capture is only `executed_unqualified`."

msgid "`validate` rebuilds unchanged admission and recipe, verifies actual operation records, protocol, instrument bytes, session, firmware/configuration, acquisition context, raw observations and sample files. It derives every result from finite, contiguous nonempty samples against the reviewed limits. Rehashed opaque protocols, null limits, missing/failed/skipped operations, stale records, changed bytes and wrong scopes fail closed. A result qualifies only the named case, selected modes and recorded conditions; it does not establish WCET, unobserved loads, certification or product release."
msgstr "`validate` rebuilds unchanged admission and recipe, verifies actual operation records, protocol, instrument bytes, session, firmware/configuration, acquisition context, raw observations and sample files. It derives every result from finite, contiguous nonempty samples against the reviewed limits. Rehashed opaque protocols, null limits, missing/failed/skipped operations, stale records, changed bytes and wrong scopes fail closed. A result qualifies only the named case, selected modes and recorded conditions; it does not establish WCET, unobserved loads, certification or product release."

msgid "Flash power-loss cases additionally require a content-pinned external product layout. The test region must use the exact part's erase boundaries, remain within physical Flash, avoid every protected region and avoid all actual firmware LOAD bytes. The external layout must protect every admitted firmware LOAD. Products own the region, protected data, power-cut safety and recovery policy. The platform reserves no default test partition and performs no destructive action during preparation, validation or commit checks."
msgstr "Flash power-loss cases additionally require a content-pinned external product layout. The test region must use the exact part's erase boundaries, remain within physical Flash, avoid every protected region and avoid all actual firmware LOAD bytes. The external layout must protect every admitted firmware LOAD. Products own the region, protected data, power-cut safety and recovery policy. The platform reserves no default test partition and performs no destructive action during preparation, validation or commit checks."

