msgstr "31"

msgid "Selected H743/U575 startup/time, GPIO/UART and finite SPI/I2C/ADC/PWM/EXTI/watchdog/Flash references. A complete peripheral set, every OS mode and actual MCU execution are not established."
msgstr "Selected H743/U575 startup/time, GPIO/UART and finite SPI/I2C/ADC/PWM/EXTI/watchdog/Flash references. A complete peripheral set, every OS mode and actual MCU execution are not established."

msgid "32"
msgstr "32"

msgid "H743 fixed cache ownership, finite USART3 DMA1 TX/RX-IDLE in selected AXI/SRAM1, separate V/HSI64 baremetal continuous RX/duplex in AXI, and an optional exact V D-Cache-off RGB565 DMA2D component; U575 finite USART1 GPDMA TX/hardware-chain TX in SRAM1 and CPU attribution mechanisms. Other unselected engines/modes and security-crossing DMA remain absent; physical coherency is unverified."
msgstr "H743 fixed cache ownership, finite USART3 DMA1 TX/RX-IDLE in selected AXI/SRAM1, separate V/HSI64 baremetal continuous RX/duplex in AXI, and an optional exact V D-Cache-off RGB565 DMA2D component; U575 finite USART1 GPDMA TX/hardware-chain TX in SRAM1 and CPU attribution mechanisms. Other unselected engines/modes and security-crossing DMA remain absent; physical coherency is unverified."

msgid "33"
msgstr "33"

msgid "Partial exact F407VET6/ZGT6 baremetal reference: explicit ClockDomain owner barrier, masked Flash vector/MSP/PC admission and nonreturning ARM tail transfer. Unknown/live RTOS or active-FP state, H743/cache handoff and other entry modes reject; full original exits and physical handoff remain open. The U575 cold world transition does not enlarge this subset."
msgstr "Partial exact F407VET6/ZGT6 baremetal reference: explicit ClockDomain owner barrier, masked Flash vector/MSP/PC admission and nonreturning ARM tail transfer. Unknown/live RTOS or active-FP state, H743/cache handoff and other entry modes reject; full original exits and physical handoff remain open. The U575 cold world transition does not enlarge this subset."

msgid "34"
msgstr "34"

msgid "Not implemented. H743's four profiles are cold configurations, with no running frequency transition, consumer reclocking or deadline-domain conversion."
msgstr "Not implemented. H743's four profiles are cold configurations, with no running frequency transition, consumer reclocking or deadline-domain conversion."

msgid "35"
msgstr "35"

msgid "Partial exact U575 TZEN0 baremetal software reference: independent retained RTC elapsed clock, explicit WUT owner, closed/joined RUN domain, verified wake access profile and retained failed-drain effects. Default Core TIM2 deadlines are invalid after stop. LPDMA/LPBAM, physical retention/accuracy/current/wake acceptance and the full original exit remain open."
msgstr "Partial exact U575 TZEN0 baremetal software reference: independent retained RTC elapsed clock, explicit WUT owner, closed/joined RUN domain, verified wake access profile and retained failed-drain effects. Default Core TIM2 deadlines are invalid after stop. LPDMA/LPBAM, physical retention/accuracy/current/wake acceptance and the full original exit remain open."

msgid "36"
msgstr "36"

msgid "Partial synchronous U575 reference only: Secure/NS images, cold attribution owner, single unprivileged NS Thread and copied GPIO gateway. No dual-world platform factory, NS RTOS, multitask identity, mutable address space, asynchronous borrow/drain or HIL isolation qualification."
msgstr "Partial synchronous U575 reference only: Secure/NS images, cold attribution owner, single unprivileged NS Thread and copied GPIO gateway. No dual-world platform factory, NS RTOS, multitask identity, mutable address space, asynchronous borrow/drain or HIL isolation qualification."

msgid "Implementing rejection of an unsupported configuration is a valid defensive contract; it is not implementation of the rejected feature. Additional features need exact controller/mode ownership and acceptance evidence before these ledger entries can close. Current first-release devices retain their declared fixed profiles."
msgstr "Implementing rejection of an unsupported configuration is a valid defensive contract; it is not implementation of the rejected feature. Additional features need exact controller/mode ownership and acceptance evidence before these ledger entries can close. Current first-release devices retain their declared fixed profiles."

msgid "The remaining software work for SOC-33–35 requires coordinated ownership rather than another profile label. The exact F407 masked handoff now implements outgoing owner/state admission and the terminal transfer. Incoming-image integration, current-source qualification and physical execution remain separate; broader running-state adoption still needs its own image/resource and FP/IRQ/cache/RAM contract. External products retain loader authentication, partition and recovery policy. Dynamic frequency changes need actual consumer quiescence, ordered electrical changes, bounded rollback, OS timing adaptation and an explicit continuous time contract. Deep STOP additionally needs an exact RTC/LPTIM reference, wake/retention admission, elapsed-time reconstruction and consumer restoration; ordinary shallow-sleep preparation does not establish it."
msgstr "The remaining software work for SOC-33–35 requires coordinated ownership rather than another profile label. The exact F407 masked handoff now implements outgoing owner/state admission and the terminal transfer. Incoming-image integration, current-source qualification and physical execution remain separate; broader running-state adoption still needs its own image/resource and FP/IRQ/cache/RAM contract. External products retain loader authentication, partition and recovery policy. Dynamic frequency changes need actual consumer quiescence, ordered electrical changes, bounded rollback, OS timing adaptation and an explicit continuous time contract. Deep STOP additionally needs an exact RTC/LPTIM reference, wake/retention admission, elapsed-time reconstruction and consumer restoration; ordinary shallow-sleep preparation does not establish it."

msgid "SOC-36 still needs a separately reviewed dual-world configuration/factory path, trusted OS task identity and mutable-map/copy-fault contracts before general userspace support. Async and DMA extensions must preserve borrow, cancel, drain and final-publication rules across the security boundary. These are additional mechanisms, not consequences of the current synchronous GPIO reference."
msgstr "SOC-36 still needs a separately reviewed dual-world configuration/factory path, trusted OS task identity and mutable-map/copy-fault contracts before general userspace support. Async and DMA extensions must preserve borrow, cancel, drain and final-publication rules across the security boundary. These are additional mechanisms, not consequences of the current synchronous GPIO reference."

msgid "Physical equipment is currently disconnected. SOC-37–55 have executable tooling and station-binding obligations; their physical exit status remains `not_executed`. See [HIL authoring and commands](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/hil/README.md)."
msgstr "Physical equipment is currently disconnected. SOC-37–55 have executable tooling and station-binding obligations; their physical exit status remains `not_executed`. See [HIL authoring and commands](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/hil/README.md)."
